# Moto G20 (java) IMS/VoWiFi cluster (2026-09-23): restored as a SET.
# These are the Unisoc IMS/VoWiFi implementation (ImsService + MMTEL +
# emergency MMTEL via vendor.sprd.hardware.radio.ims@1.0::IImsRadio, WFC
# user plane, RadioInteractor extended-RIL bridge). NOT replaceable by
# Lineage (framework provides only the ImsService client). They share
# android.uid.phone with TeleService/TelephonyProvider — coexistence works
# because the generated Android.bp modules carry certificate: "platform"
# (verified: staged APKs are platform-cert-signed, matching TeleService).
# Excluded (Motorola-signed, shared-UID conflicts, optional features):
#   CallFireWall LinkTurbo USCPhotosProvider VceDaemon UniTelephony Omacp
#   (USCPhotosProvider was the "Signature mismatch" crash source on
#   android.media/10077).
# NOTE: radio_interactor_service runs INSIDE the com.android.phone process
# (android:process="com.android.phone") and needs the Unisoc SDK classes
# (UtilLog, RadioInteractor) — provided on the boot classpath via
# PRODUCT_BOOT_JARS (see lineage_java.mk + the dex_import modules in
# device/motorola/java/Android.bp). 2026-09-23.
PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
    ims \
    ImsCM \
    SprdVoWifiService \
    SprdVoWifiConfiguration \
    radio_interactor_service \
    android.hardware.bluetooth@1.1-service.unisoc \
    android.hardware.gatekeeper@1.0-service.trusty

